      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add gated Claw discovery and API projection",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add enabled Claw discovery through the existing package list, search, detail, and version APIs\n- accept `family=claw` only when `CLAWHUB_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\n- project the non-sensitive `clawManifestSummary` on package and version responses\n- keep plugin category and trending filters plugin-only\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Depends on: #3090\n- This is ClawHub PR 3 of 4. It remains draft and experimental.\n- Next: hosted feed export and published-package E2E through OpenClaw dry-run.\n\n## Contract\n\nThis slice is the additive discovery surface. PR #3090 owns the fail-closed read boundary and public release serializer: disabled deployments omit Claws from unscoped results, reject explicit Claw filters, hide named reads, and never expose `extractedClawManifest`. This PR adds enabled list/search/detail/version behavior and exposes only the safe summary.\n\nThe API reuses `/api/v1/packages` rather than creating a parallel registry contract. The `claw` family remains explicitly unstable and available only behind the deployment gate while the RFC and stack are under review.\n\n## Validation\n\n- focused gate, Convex package, HTTP, and schema suites: 680 tests\n- `bun run ci:types-build`\n- `bun run ci:static`\n- structured Codex review against the updated #3090 head: clean, no actionable findings\n\nNo reusable local Convex deployment was available for a live enabled/disabled transcript. PR #3092 provides the coordinated hosted-package download and real OpenClaw `claws add --dry-run` proof; the deployment flag must remain off until the complete experimental stack is present.",
